 "capsule": "In this 1260–1415 window the Margraviate of Brandenburg was the Ascanian-ruled March of the Holy Roman Empire, expanding to the Oder before the dynasty's extinction in 1320 plunged it into disputed Wittelsbach and Luxembourg overlordship. The 1356 Golden Bull made its ruler a permanent imperial Elector, and in 1415 Emperor Sigismund granted the march to Frederick VI of Nuremberg, founding five centuries of Hohenzollern rule.",
